# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rust build output
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This machine sets a shared `target-dir` in ~/.cargo/config.toml, so a local ./target may
# never appear — ignored anyway so this file stays correct on a machine that doesn't.
/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# amb's own runtime state — never commit a board
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The real board lives at ~/.agent-messageboard/board.db, outside every repo (D11, D15), so in
# normal use nothing here ever appears. This guard is for the one-keystroke accident: every doc
# and test drives the binary through `AMB_DB=...`, and `AMB_DB=./t.db` drops a board straight
# into the working tree. Committing one is worse than useless — DESIGN.md: a lease in git
# history "reads as current". Claims carry a wall-clock `expires_at` (D13), so a checked-in
# board hands a reader claims that expired before they cloned it.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# `amb install` writes this beside any settings.json it edits, including under a test HOME.
*.amb-backup

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Verification tooling
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLAUDE.md makes mutation testing a standing convention ("after adding a guard, delete it and
# watch the test go red"). cargo-mutants writes its scratch tree and report here.
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# cargo-llvm-cov / grcov
*.profraw
*.profdata
/coverage
lcov.info

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# bench/ — the Python startup and queue harnesses behind MEASUREMENTS.md
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editors and OS
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# devt plugin (carried over from the devt-generated ignore file)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# workflow state (recursive — catches sub-tree devt invocations)
**/.devt/state/
# agent persistent memory (per-project)
.claude/agent-memory/
# memory FTS5 index (regenerable from the markdown beside it)
.devt/memory/index.db
# memory auto-index debounce marker (transient)
.devt/memory/.auto-index-stamp
# MCP tool-call trace (recursive)
**/.devt/memory/_mcp-trace.jsonl
# memory export bundles (transient — share through an explicit channel)
.devt/memory/export-*.json

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# graphify — entirely derived from src/
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# graph.json and graph.html are ~944K together, roughly 10x all the hand-written source, and
# both are regenerated from src/ by graphify. Tracking them makes every source edit produce an
# unreviewable diff, and a graph that drifts silently out of date is worse than no graph.
# Regenerate with /graphify.
#
# To keep the graph for fresh clones instead — so the graphify MCP server in .mcp.json resolves
# without a regen — replace this line with `graphify-out/cache/` + `graphify-out/manifest.json`.
graphify-out/

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deliberately NOT ignored
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Listed because an un-ignored file looks exactly like a forgotten one, and these get
# "helpfully" fixed otherwise.
#
#   Cargo.lock          committed. `amb` is a binary with `publish = false`; applications commit
#                       their lockfile so a build is reproducible. Not a library.
#   rust-toolchain.toml committed. rustup has no global default on this machine, so this file is
#                       the only reason `cargo` resolves inside this directory at all.
#   .devt/rules/        committed. Shared conventions, not local state.
#   .claude/settings.json, .mcp.json
#                       committed. Project config, no secrets and no absolute paths.
#   src/schema.sql      committed. It is source, not output — `*.db` above must never grow to
#                       cover `*.sql`.

# Claude Code local settings — per-machine hook config, deliberately not shared.
# `.claude/settings.json` above IS committed (project config); this one is the local override
# and carries absolute binary paths, so it must never be.
.claude/settings.local.json
